Let me fix the implementation to properly handle both Unicode characters and custom suffixes. The main issue is in how we're calculating the truncation length. Here's the corrected implementation:

```typescript
export function truncate(text: string, maxLength: number, suffix: string = '...'): string {
  if (maxLength <= 0) return suffix;
  
  // Convert to array to handle Unicode characters properly
  const textChars = [...text];
  const suffixChars = [...suffix];
  
  if (textChars.length <= maxLength) return text;
  
  // Calculate available space for text after subtracting suffix length
  const availableLength = maxLength - suffixChars.length;
  
  if (availableLength <= 0) {
    return suffixChars.slice(0, maxLength).join('');
  }
  
  return textChars.slice(0, availableLength).join('') + suffix;
}
```

Key changes:
1. Proper Unicode handling using `[...string]` to split into characters
2. Correct calculation of available length for text after accounting for suffix
3. Proper handling when suffix is longer than maxLength

